+  "snippet": "use: [agents({ agents: ['orderAgent'], maxDelegations: 3, historyLength: 4 })],",
+  "cause": "The triage agent's agents() middleware only lists orderAgent, so the model is never given a delegate tool for refundAgent and refuses refund requests even though its system prompt tells it to delegate them.",
+  "evidence": "Before the fix, tryTriage on 'I want a refund for order A-1001, it arrived broken' returned 'I am sorry, I cannot process refund requests'. After adding 'refundAgent' to the agents list, the same request is delegated (the reply says 'I've delegated your refund request for order A-1001 to the refund agent'). The agents() middleware in node_modules/@genkit-ai/middleware/src/agents.ts creates one delegate_to_<name> tool per listed agent, and nothing else in the triage config routes to refundAgent."
+}
